# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER commit game data.  This project ships tools and analysis only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rom/*
!rom/README.md
build/
build-native/
build*/
assets/extracted/
vendor/asar/
vendor/asar-build/
build-native/
build*/
*.sfc
*.smc
*.srm
*.bin
__pycache__/
*.pyc
rom/music/
rom/sfx/

# Scratch.  NOTHING that is needed may live here - the labs read from
# assets/rips (hand-supplied sheets) and assets/captures (live dumps).
tmp/
error.log

# Game artwork and live memory dumps: local only, same rule as rom/.
assets/rips/*
!assets/rips/README.md
assets/captures/*
!assets/captures/README.md

# MAME save states hold the console's RAM and VRAM - game data; keep them local
tools/labs/mame/sessions/snes/

# Training output: checkpoints and exported input traces.  A .pads file is
# a policy's own button presses, not game data, but it is a build product
# and there is no reason for it in the tree.
runs/
*.pads
*.pt

# The policy compiled into the game (tools/rl/embed_net.py).  These are
# learned parameters and not ROM bytes, but they were trained entirely
# against the cartridge's physics and racing lines and they encode how to
# drive them - closer to the line this project draws than anything else
# in the tree.  So it is GENERATED, never committed, and shipping it is a
# decision to take deliberately rather than by accident.
src/netpolicy.inc
